        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sdmH2Lh8s6HiHu3jjXA6-22" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;1. Stack Memory&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stack Memory is the place where all primitive variables, methods and object references are stored.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Whenever a project executions starts, JVM pushes the method, variables and created object reference in heap memory will be store one by one to the stack.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Methods will be pushed first in the stack and it defines scope within the stack memory where method level variables and references will be stored.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Each method scope is isolated with other method scopes. Meaning variables, object references etc won&#39;t know about variables and object references stored in another method scope.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Each Thread will have it&#39;s own stack memory but share common heap memory and metaspace.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;When method executions finishes, then method scope will be destroyed in LIFO order.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;When Stack memory became full, JVM will throw StackOverFlowError.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="640" x="80" y="1240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sdmH2Lh8s6HiHu3jjXA6-23" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;text-align: left; margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;JVM Memory in Depth&lt;/h1&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="480" x="150" y="1190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
